Subject: [PATCH] cpuset, cpuacct: let a CAP_SYS_NICE process move other users' tasks

A cgroup v1 lets a process move a task of another user only if every controller in
the hierarchy allows it through allow_attach. In this kernel only the cpu controller
has the hook (subsys_cgroup_allow_attach, which asks for CAP_SYS_NICE). Android's
later common kernels have it on cpuset as well; this gives it to cpuset and cpuacct.

cpuset: system_server, which runs as system and holds CAP_SYS_NICE, moves every app
between /dev/cpuset/foreground, background, top-app and the rest as its state
changes. Each move was refused ("AddTidToCgroup failed to write ...: Permission
denied" on cgroup.procs, hundreds of times in a day of Android 13's logs), and apps
stayed in the cpuset they started in.

cpuacct: with no cgroup v2, the per-app process groups are a cpuacct hierarchy
(rom/device/asus/ASUS_P00I/tools/tree-patches/system/core/0001). Zygote puts its
children there while still root; for WebView's and the app zygotes' children,
system_server does it, and without the hook it would be refused.
---
--- kernel/cpuset.c
+++ kernel/cpuset.c
@@ -1969,6 +1969,7 @@
 	.css_offline = cpuset_css_offline,
 	.css_free = cpuset_css_free,
 	.can_attach = cpuset_can_attach,
+	.allow_attach = subsys_cgroup_allow_attach,
 	.cancel_attach = cpuset_cancel_attach,
 	.attach = cpuset_attach,
 	.subsys_id = cpuset_subsys_id,
--- kernel/sched/cpuacct.c
+++ kernel/sched/cpuacct.c
@@ -290,6 +290,7 @@
 	.name		= "cpuacct",
 	.css_alloc	= cpuacct_css_alloc,
 	.css_free	= cpuacct_css_free,
+	.allow_attach	= subsys_cgroup_allow_attach,
 	.subsys_id	= cpuacct_subsys_id,
 	.base_cftypes	= files,
 	.early_init	= 1,
